## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

**Chủ đề: vì sao mã trạng thái HTTP quan trọng.**

> *"This sounds like a small thing but it's the API decision I feel most strongly about, because I spent three years on the receiving end of it.*
> *The pattern I kept hitting was an API that returns 200 OK with an error object in the body. Every single call site then needs to check two things — did the request succeed, and did the operation succeed. People forget the second check. Bugs ship.*
> *So in my API the status code is always honest. The client checks whether the response is ok, and if it isn't, there's a structured error with a stable machine-readable code.*
> *The reason the code is separate from the message: the code is a contract and never changes, the message is human-facing and I want to be able to reword it without breaking an app that's already installed on someone's phone. That's a mobile-specific concern — I can't force everyone to update.*
> *One more thing I'd mention: 403 versus 404. Returning 403 for someone else's record confirms it exists, which leaks information. For anything sensitive I return 404 for both cases."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `on the receiving end` | ở phía phải hứng chịu | *I was on the receiving end of it.* |
| `call site` | chỗ gọi hàm | *Every call site needs two checks.* |
| `honest` (về mã lỗi) | phản ánh đúng sự thật | *The status code is always honest.* |
| `reword` (v) | viết lại câu chữ | *I want to reword it without breaking anything.* |
| `leak information` | rò rỉ thông tin | *Returning 403 leaks information.* |

